t('11 · N07/N08: originals and waveforms',p('N07 asks whether a source is authentic, permitted and suitable. N08 asks whether a supported recording can be parsed, preserved and replayed without losing identity or time. A hash is a fingerprint of bytes: matching it helps detect alteration, but does not prove scientific correctness or usage rights.')+table(['Retained original / status','What it actually provides'],[['NASA NTRS 20205008796 metadata','7 KB catalog record for the 2020 market survey of commercial clinical decision-support/wellness tools; not the full publication or patient data.'],['OSD-1 / GLDS-1 metadata','About 8 KB describing a fruit-fly expression study associated with STS-121; no acquired raw expression/omics samples.'],['PhysioNet BIDMC 01 numerics','7,644-byte authentic de-identified public clinical numerics CSV; relative 0–480 s, 1 s cadence, monitor-derived HR/pulse/respiration/SpO₂ fields. Offline archive only.'],['Sleep-EDF SC4001 source requirement','No accepted PSG/annotation pair. A partial 1,146,508-byte PSG transfer is not the expected 48,338,048-byte complete source and is not qualified.'],['N13 two NASA PDFs','Separate approved publication corpus; full titles and identities appear on page 17.']],[38,62])+h('The waveform engineering path')+p('The current N08 parser accepts its own explicitly synthetic ASTRAWV1 binary and ASTRACSVv1 CSV contracts. Metadata defines source, crew, channels, units, start time and rate. Binary samples use bounded float32 data; normalization preserves source/channel identity. Original bytes and 1–5 second channel chunks are stored with hashes in SQLite BLOBs, not re-created as a fabricated “live” stream.')+flow('Figure T7. Archive time and knowledge time both govern replay.',['Authorized synthetic file + explicit provenance confirmation','Validate size, schema, rate, units, channels and finite samples','Commit original source + hashed chunks atomically','Read bounded channel window at eligible cutoff','Render extrema / gaps / quality → seek and play archive time'])+p('Limits include 256,000 bytes, 1–60 s, 1–3 channels, 50–500 Hz, 64 revisions and 8 MiB per crew payload. Missing intervals remain missing. Experimental peaks are descriptive engineering outputs; PPG is not converted into a validated blood-pressure reading. N08’s original inactive timing descriptor and N06’s separately authorized archive reader should not be confused.')+p('BIDMC usage rights retain ODC-By 1.0 and original notices; the card records that publisher-checksum verification is false. Single-record scope cannot supply independent clinical train/test evidence. Authentic source availability, anatomical linkage review and missing named sources remain external acceptance gates.')+refs('data/scientific/n07-local-registry.json','data/scientific/bidmc/BIDMC-01.dataset-card.json','packages/waveforms.mjs','services/waveforms/service.mjs'),'compact','ch11')
t('12 · N09: how fictional readings are made',p('A simulator is a controlled generator. ASTRA does not choose an arbitrary number every time a card is drawn. A seeded pseudo-random generator, authored personal references, circadian variation, noise and scenario effects produce reproducible source-time observations. Software can then commit and replay them through the real pipeline.')+h('Six fictional crew, independent assignments')+table(['Crew','Identity'],[['CREW-01 / VEGA','Elena Voss · Commander'],['CREW-02 / ATLAS','Marcus Chen · Mission pilot'],['CREW-03 / NOVA','Amara Okafor · Science officer'],['CREW-04 / KITE','Yuki Tanaka · Systems engineer'],['CREW-05 / SOL','Rafael Costa · Medical officer'],['CREW-06 / LYRA','Noor Hassan · Communications specialist']],[40,60])+p('The generator version is <code>n09-source-time-v1</code>. Calibration archives use 720 hourly draws per metric—30 authored days—not 30 days of measured astronaut data. A default seed of 42017 plus crew-specific structure supports repeatability. Box–Muller-style Gaussian sampling and repository arithmetic are implementation choices, not learned physiology.')+flow('Figure T8. A scenario genuinely exercises monitoring, persistence and the UI.',['Start versioned cardiorespiratory-drift run for CREW-03','Generate cadence-bound HR / respiration / SpO₂ changes','Commit observations → N02 quality + persistence rules','Persist qualified risk event → snapshot / API / browser','Human acknowledgement → durable delayed report'])+h('Scheduling, quality and replay')+p('Runs permit defined cadences (30, 60, 300, 1,800 or 3,600 seconds) and bounded durations up to seven days, with frame/run limits. Real-time progression and manual advance both move mission time. Pause holds progression; sources can become stale. Stop retains evidence; reset creates new execution history. Versioned events and request IDs prevent duplicate commands.')+p('The ten presets are nominal, controlled-hr-rise, cardiorespiratory-drift, sleep-debt-cardio-drift, sleep-fatigue, post-exercise, radiation-spike, sensor-dropout, contradictory-sensors and communication-blackout. Some alter quality or communications rather than physiology. Scenario replay respects what source/record was known at the cutoff, so later reset state must not leak into an earlier view. This is a test generator, not a physical wearable or validated disease model.')+refs('services/telemetry-simulator/simulator.mjs','services/telemetry-simulator/n09-model.mjs','services/telemetry-simulator/n09-engine.mjs','apps/mission-control-web/n09.mjs'),'compact','ch12')
t('13 · N10: sleep, exercise and cognition',p('N10 combines non-private mission context with optional private personal inputs. Its important distinction is between <strong>describing records</strong> and <strong>diagnosing a condition</strong>. The implementation can count sleep duration or exercise adherence without proving that a particular person has a clinical disorder.')+h('Versioned records instead of silent edits')+p('The ledger appends revisions with crew identity, record kind, source time and knowledge time. Sleep intervals, stages and schedules support completed-duration and coverage calculations. A later correction changes the eligible projection without rewriting an earlier original. Historical views consider when that correction became known.')+table(['Record / calculation','Meaning and limitation'],[['Sleep sessions and stages','Completed intervals, available stage labels and gaps; stage availability is not a new sleep-classification model.'],['Schedule and descriptive shortfall','Compare a plan with eligible recorded sleep. A shortfall is an accounting result, not a medical sleep-debt diagnosis.'],['Exercise plan / session / movement','Track duration, workload context, adherence and available movement entries; not a personalized treatment prescription.'],['Reaction task','Five voluntary timed trials with readiness/false-start handling; a personal reference requires enough eligible same-person observations.'],['Mood / fatigue input','Optional self-report under consent; not a psychiatric or clinical cognitive score.'],['Review sharing and privacy','Current consent plus actor/device and role rules determine visibility. Historical timestamps alone do not bypass current privacy restrictions.']],[35,65])+flow('Figure T9. Research context does not automatically become an operational medical decision.',['Consent / authorized non-private context intake','Validate source + actor + crew + revision + time','Append record → rebuild eligible projection','Sleep/exercise view or private personal history','Only permitted non-private context reaches N06 / N09'])+p('The Sleep &amp; resilience screen implements the allowed forms and history. The voluntary cognitive utility is separate. N06’s conceptual head context can describe completed non-private sleep but must not expose another actor’s reaction trials or mood. Missing coverage, insufficient personal reference, denied sharing and revoked consent remain explicit unavailable states.')+h('Why the dual clock matters')+p('A session may end yesterday but be entered today. Yesterday’s replay must not pretend the system already knew it. Source time and knowledge time solve different questions.')+refs('services/n10/contracts.mjs','services/n10/ledger.mjs','services/n10/projection.mjs','apps/mission-control-web/n10.mjs','docs/N10_CONTRACT.md'),'compact','ch13')
t('14 · N11: anomaly evaluation and rejection',p('An <strong>anomaly</strong> is an observation unusual relative to a reference. Unusual does not mean disease. N02 uses fixed review rules; N11 compares advanced candidate methods in a separate research/shadow evaluation. A candidate never earns operational authority just because its code runs.')+h('Three kinds of research logic')+table(['Method','Simple explanation / implementation role'],[['Robust personal reference','Describe a person’s baseline and scale before scoring changes; source quality and eligible history matter.'],['EWMA','Exponentially weighted moving average gives more weight to recent values while remembering older ones. It can emphasize sustained drift.'],['Isolation Forest','Build random partition trees. A point isolated after fewer splits may be more unusual than points requiring many splits. It is not a supervised medical-diagnosis model.']],[32,68])+h('How Isolation Forest works')+p('Imagine repeatedly splitting a scatterplot with randomly chosen features and cut points. A lone remote point is often separated quickly. A dense cluster usually takes more cuts. The algorithm averages path lengths and converts them to a rarity score. Its usefulness depends on feature scaling, population, quality, training distribution and a defensible evaluation design.')+p('ASTRA implements candidate research logic in repository JavaScript, including reference fitting, feature extraction, EWMA and forest scoring. This is not evidence of a hidden online AI service or a currently deployed scikit-learn detector. Research job/result/event records preserve policies and outcomes so failed results are not erased.')+h('The actual outcome matters more than the model name')+box('<strong>Isolation Forest was rejected:</strong> the retained synthetic evaluation reports 0 true positives and 4 false negatives on four authored detection cases, plus 44 false episodes on the already-seen robustness material. It remains rejected/disabled. The four misses must not be presented as a successful detector.',True)+p('Tier A/EWMA outcomes on four authored events do not establish clinical sensitivity either. Authored cases are engineering controls, not independent real-patient outcomes. Choosing or tuning a model after seeing those cases also prevents relabeling that set as unseen validation.')+h('What the application may show')+p('Evidence &amp; provenance exposes scoped model evidence and saved research state to permitted roles. It must preserve REJECTED / NOT_PROMOTED labels. The active N02 alert authority remains deterministic monitoring. Starting another candidate fit or research worker is not part of this documentation or presentation scope.')+refs('services/n11/algorithms.mjs → fitReferences/featurePoint/fitForest/forestScore','services/n11/experiment.mjs','services/n11/service.mjs','docs/N11_FINAL_ENGINEERING_COMPLETION.md'),'compact','ch14')
t('15 · N12: understanding forecasts',p('A <strong>forecast</strong> estimates a later value from earlier observations. It is not a diagnosis or a guarantee. ASTRA implements three understandable methods so candidate complexity can be compared with a trustworthy baseline. Its research answers can legitimately be UNKNOWN.')+table(['Method','How it works','Illustrative next value'],[['Persistence','Repeat the last eligible value. A strong baseline when there is little dependable trend.','60, 62, 64 → 64'],['OLS / linear','Ordinary Least Squares chooses the line minimizing squared vertical errors. Fit value = intercept + slope × time.','At times 0,1,2: 60,62,64 → at 3: 66'],['Theil–Sen / robust','Compute pairwise slopes; take the median slope and a median intercept. Often less sensitive to isolated outliers than OLS, but not immune to bad data.','Same clean sequence → slope 2 → at 3: 66']],[22,53,25])+p('These are arithmetic examples, not crew readings or validated clinical forecasts. A forecast can fail even when a fitted line looks smooth. The future may change, samples may be missing and the apparent trend may be an artifact.')+flow('Figure T10. The full research protocol separates references, calibration and evaluation.',['Eligible chronological, same-person source observations','Fit persistence / OLS / Theil–Sen candidate','Calibrate residual interval on separate eligible history','Evaluate later issue times / horizons without future leakage','Store evidence + policy identity → qualified / rejected / UNKNOWN'])+h('Coverage, horizons and reference units')+p('The full N12 protocol checks a bounded recent history, good coverage, metric units, source/knowledge cutoffs and a current sample. Horizons are 5, 15, 30 and 60 minutes. It standardizes against a same-person mean and sample standard deviation using n−1, unlike N02’s robust median/MAD reference. These scales must not be described interchangeably.')+h('Two implementations you should distinguish')+p('The application also retains <code>services/prediction/forecast.mjs</code>, a legacy conditional trend helper using an existing calibration record. It requires enough eligible history and can abstain. The full N12 experiment, registry and saved research UI live under <code>services/n12/</code>. Seeing a legacy trend card does not mean the complete N12 evaluation just ran.')+refs('services/n12/forecast.mjs → reference, forecast methods','services/n12/experiment.mjs','services/prediction/forecast.mjs','models/forecast-calibration.json'),'compact','ch15')
t('15 · Forecast evidence, not promises',h('Intervals and abstention')+p('N12 forms empirical residual-based intervals using a calibration quantile aimed at nominal 90% coverage. The rank is based on ceil((n+1)×0.9), with a minimum calibration count. This is a target of the procedure, not a guarantee that every metric/horizon achieved 90% coverage, and not a confidence percentage that a person is safe.')+p('The pipeline rejects or withholds output for inadequate coverage, stale sources, incompatible units/policies, future or duplicate timestamps, unavailable selection, rejected candidates and unsupported extrapolation. A finite output from a simple formula is not enough to qualify the answer.')+h('What the frozen synthetic registry actually says')+table(['Registry class','Count / exact interpretation'],[['ENGINEERING_BASELINE','8 baseline cells retained for comparison.'],['ENGINEERING_QUALIFIED_SYNTHETIC_ONLY','4 cells: linear:hrv:5; robust:heart_rate:5; robust:heart_rate:15; robust:hrv:5.'],['REJECTED_FOR_ADDITIONAL_USE','12 cells. These remain rejected instead of being relabeled to improve the report.'],['Operational promotion','0. Independent use approval remains absent.']],[43,57])+h('Time leakage: a common false success')+p('A forecast issued at 12:00 must not use a measurement first known at 12:10. That would show it the future and falsely improve its score. ASTRA binds issue/source/knowledge time, partitions and selection availability.')+flow('Figure T11. Different eligibility decisions must not collapse into a single “AI accuracy” number.',['Training / reference period → freeze method identity','Calibration period → determine interval rule','Later evaluation period → measure errors and coverage','Independent scientific / use review remains a separate gate'])+h('How to present this safely')+p('Show saved evidence, the method name, horizon, actual coverage/quality and a truthful available or UNKNOWN result. Say “qualified on authored synthetic engineering cases” rather than “medically reliable prediction.” Current presentation authority does not permit fresh Compute, calibration, evaluation or promotion. The N12 and N11 research interfaces to operational N16 remain inactive.')+box('<strong>Registry provenance:</strong> the exact counts above come from the retained 24-cell model registry, not a new evaluation performed for these PDFs. Model files and history have not been changed.')+refs('artifacts/n12-engineering-20261104/execution-01/model-registry.json','services/n12/forecast.mjs','services/n12/service.mjs','docs/N12_FINAL_ENGINEERING_COMPLETION.md'),'compact')
t('16 · N13: the NASA evidence corpus',p('A reliable citation must resolve to the original publication, not an internally generated summary. N13 preserves original bytes and exact source spans. Its 33 evidence units map to 34 exact windows because evidence units and source spans are different objects. The forty evaluation questions remain seen/provisional, with zero independent question approvals.')+h('Publication 1 · sleep, circadian timing and workload')+p('<strong>Risk of Performance Decrements and Adverse Health Outcomes Resulting from Sleep Loss, Circadian Desynchronization, and Work Overload.</strong> Authors recorded: Erin Flynn-Evans, Kevin Gregory, Lucia Arsintescu and Alexandra Whitmire. Publisher: NASA Human Research Program / Johnson Space Center; NTRS 20160003864; JSC-CN-35774. Version: 2016; catalogued date 2016-01-01. The exact publication day is not independently established by this documentation review.')+p('<a href="https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20160003864">ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20160003864</a>','small')+code('source_id: nasa-hrp-sleep-2016\nbytes: 967704\nSHA-256: 252d4993a040ab8b989664b1da7a3143a5fd8169fac65b67f1f43231250ef1f5')+h('Publication 2 · human-system standard')+p('<strong>NASA Spaceflight Human-System Standard, Volume 2: Human Factors, Habitability, and Environmental Health.</strong> Institutional author: NASA Office of the Chief Health and Medical Officer. Publisher: NASA Technical Standards System. Local source record: Revision F, dated 2026-07-14. This is the version recorded in the repository, not a claim that this documentation checked the latest web revision.')+p('<a href="https://standards.nasa.gov/standard/NASA/NASA-STD-3001_VOL_2">standards.nasa.gov/standard/NASA/NASA-STD-3001_VOL_2</a>','small')+code('source_id: nasa-std-3001-v2-f\nbytes: 6753988\nSHA-256: a09e0a3853306f59a62b5ab494734c25afc8f83eadb159fdb5825706bc36d48f')+h('What is checked and what is not')+p('Exact example: “Further research is needed in this area” appears in the 2016 HRP report, physical PDF page 4 (original PDF page 4; text retained in data/corpus/n13-01/derived/nasa-hrp-sleep-2016.pages.json). This caveat is not a personal medical answer. The catalog records source version, locator, hash, quotation, page/section and lineage. Versioned deterministic bundles and cold verification detect altered or mismatched content. Independent relevance/applicability review remains pending; deterministic string matching cannot replace it.')+box('<strong>Rights and scientific limits:</strong> original notices remain attached; no blanket license for third-party works cited inside NASA documents is inferred. Publications support attribution and research context, not automatic medical recommendations or NASA endorsement. The bibliography links above are locally recorded canonical references, not newly browsed sources.')+refs('data/corpus/n13-01/sources.json','services/corpus/sources.mjs','services/corpus/catalog.mjs','services/corpus/catalog-bundle.mjs','scripts/n13-corpus.mjs'),'compact','ch16')
t('17 · N14: find evidence offline',p('<strong>Retrieval</strong> finds existing text. It does not generate a new scientific answer. N14 consumes the pinned N13 corpus: stable IDs, source hashes and exact windows must agree before results can be trusted as authentic quotations. The operational research baseline remains deterministic lexical lookup.')+table(['Method','Plain-language example / current state'],[['Lexical','For “light circadian sleep”, rank source windows with matching informative terms and fixed term weighting. Stable tie-breaking makes repeats reproducible. Current permitted baseline.'],['Semantic / MiniLM','Represent query and window meanings as vectors. A phrase such as “body-clock disruption” may be near “circadian desynchronization” without the same words. Research candidate; fresh native inference is authorization-blocked.'],['Hybrid','Combine lexical and semantic ranks or append eligible semantic rescue results without duplicating windows. Versioned implementations work as research diagnostics; not promoted.']],[27,73])+h('What is a 384-dimensional embedding?')+p('Embeddings represent text numerically: MiniLM emits 384 values. Tokenization creates model inputs; masked mean pooling combines tokens; normalization controls vector length. Cosine similarity compares directions, not truth.')+p('The pinned candidate is <strong>Xenova/all-MiniLM-L6-v2</strong>, revision <code>751bff37182d3f1213fa05d7196b954e230abad9</code>. The research encoder uses local quantized ONNX assets, ONNX Runtime 1.21.0 and tokenizers 0.2.0. Asset identity is established in retained records; independent numerical parity remains UNVERIFIED. Running the same implementation twice cannot establish independent parity.')+flow('Figure T12. Attribution and support are separate gates.',['Query + approved source scope + fixed policy','Validate corpus/windows → rank top-K evidence','Verify document + window + exact quotation / citation','Question relevance / entailment / numeric support: separate','Unsupported factual question → ABSTAIN, not a cited invention'])+p('Citation statuses are ACCEPT for exact attribution, REJECT for altered/wrong-source quotes and ABSTAIN when context is missing. This does not establish relevance. All forty questions remain seen/provisional; their metrics cannot justify promotion.')+code('node scripts/n14-offline.mjs verify\nnode scripts/n14-offline.mjs query --policy=rich_lexical \\\n  --top_k=3 --query="light circadian sleep"')+refs('services/research-retrieval/retrieval.mjs','services/research-retrieval/encoder.mjs','services/research-retrieval/research-service.mjs','docs/N14_FINAL_ENGINEERING_COMPLETION.md'),'compact','ch17')
t('18 · N15: local generative AI, governed',p('A <strong>large language model (LLM)</strong> predicts and generates text. It can produce fluent false statements, known as hallucinations. Qwen is the model family used in ASTRA’s local generation research. The main application does not currently run Qwen to answer medical questions.')+table(['Pinned component','Actual identity'],[['Model','Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct; Qwen/Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct-GGUF.'],['Revision / file','9217f5db79a29953eb74d5343926648285ec7e67 / qwen2.5-0.5b-instruct-q4_k_m.gguf.'],['Size / hash','491,400,032 bytes; SHA-256 74a4da8c9fdbcd15bd1f6d01d621410d31c6fc00986f5eb687824e7b93d7a9db.'],['Runtime','llama.cpp b11669 / v0.7.0; commit 620d2225cc436ab0b001e3200e590e3b286ef9ab.'],['Current admission','MODEL_NOT_AUTHORIZED; startup budget 0. Old grants and retained weights do not renew resource/sandbox permission.']],[27,73])+p('<strong>GGUF</strong> packages local model data. <strong>Q4_K_M quantization</strong> uses mixed low-bit weight blocks to reduce resources, with possible quality trade-offs. It does not confer medical expertise. A local model needs no OpenAI or cloud-Qwen API key, but it still needs allowed RAM/CPU/storage, safe runtime configuration and current execution authority.')+flow('Figure T13. RAG means retrieved context before generation, followed by independent checks.',['Validate question → eligible N14 evidence + source binding','Separate attribution / relevance / factual support decisions','Bounded prompt: source text is untrusted DATA','Current native admission → generation only if authorized','Verify every output claim + citation → answer or ABSTAIN','Durable audit → cold re-verification without generation replay'])+h('What historical execution did—and did not—prove')+p('Native Qwen did run in earlier bounded research. Retained experiments include a malformed-schema result rejected after inference and a conservative abstention on a supported prompt. Those are evidence of local execution, not unrestricted factual-answer success. Recent verification checked identities with zero fresh native starts. QA providers marked generated_by_llm:false are simulations, not native execution.')+p('The accommodations rule is inactive pending independent scientific review and owner acceptance. Lifecycle metadata cannot create human approval. Without approved support, factual requests abstain. Exact source reproduction is attribution-only. Prompt injection, arbitrary paths, unsupported numbers and invented references are rejected or withheld.')+refs('services/research-answer/model-admission.mjs','services/research-answer/governed-service.mjs','services/research-answer/selection.mjs','services/research-answer/relevance.mjs','services/research-answer/support-lifecycle.mjs'),'compact','ch18')
t('19 · N16: a constrained tool coordinator',p('An <strong>agent</strong> coordinates actions or tools toward a task. A chatbot may only return text. ASTRA’s N16 prototype demonstrates a constrained, risk-first coordinator with four fixed SQL read tools against a separately authorized synthetic source. This is not a deployed autonomous doctor or an active application integration.')+table(['Tool','Input and meaningful output'],[['get_current_vitals','Crew ID plus allowed metric list → source-bound current observations, not fabricated readings.'],['get_data_quality','Same bounded crew/metric scope → missingness, freshness and quality context.'],['get_personal_baseline','Allowed crew/metrics → personal reference statistics and source identity.'],['get_open_risk_events','Crew ID and bounded limit → existing synthetic source risk records, not a new N02 alert.']],[35,65])+lanes('Figure T14. A recorded four-tool result is distinct from operational app dispatch.',[('Authorized synthetic task','Versioned coordinator + bounded tool calls','active'),('Fixed SELECT workers|Separate sealed synthetic source','Four structured results + durable audit','active'),('Recorded HTML / JSON trace','Cold recovery evidence, replay 0','active'),('Main application / N02 cases','N16 operational coordinator / dispatch','inactive')])+h('Why fixed SQL and workers?')+p('SQL reads structured database records. The constrained workers allow only specific SELECT statements, source identities, columns and bounded arguments; unexpected actions/objects are denied. A read-only connection alone is insufficient, so the fixed-select authorizer and finite worker startup permission add separate restrictions. Untrusted users cannot supply arbitrary SQL or choose a database path.')+p('The retained final engineering run used four workers, four read-only connections and four fixed SELECTs, committed 18 events and recovered COMPLETE in a cold process without re-executing the tools. Its risk record is authored synthetic, with N02 provenance UNKNOWN and actual_N02_event:false. It must not be presented as a genuine operational N02 alert.')+h('Do not confuse the two “agent” experiences')+p('The main Health Agent displays deterministic N02 case templates, marked generated_by_llm:false. Named steps do not prove N16 execution. The separate <code>artifacts/n16-final-20261030/native/demo.html</code> displays a recorded trace without workers; operational dispatch and sealed-source execution remain inactive.')+refs('services/agent/master-contract.mjs','services/agent/master-coordinator.mjs','services/agent/fixed-select-authorizer.mjs','services/agent/master-worker.mjs','services/agent/agent.mjs','docs/N16_MASTER_COMPLETION_REPORT.md'),'compact','ch19')
